        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Additional tricks. While our experiments so far have focused exclusively on vanilla row-wise quantization, we want to emphasize that GPTQ is compatible with essentially any choice of quantization grid. For example, it is easily combined with standard grouping (Alistarh et al., 2017; Park et al., 2022), i.e. applying independent quantization to groups of g consecutive weights. As shown in the last rows of Table 5, this can bring noticeable extra accuracy for the largest models at 3-bit. Further, as visualized in Figure 4, it significantly reduces the accuracy losses for medium sized models at 4-bit precision.",
            "block_bbox": [
